---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';

const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/sequenzy-vs-drip';
const title = 'Sequenzy vs Drip for Shopify Email: 2026 Comparison';
const desc = "Sequenzy vs Drip for Shopify: preserve tags and custom fields, compare workflow changes, evaluate AI assistance and scope SMS requirements before migration.";

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is Sequenzy missing a visual workflow builder?",
    "answer": "No. Its current feature matrix lists a visual automation builder alongside AI assistance. Compare the resulting logic and editing process rather than assuming it only accepts prompts."
  },
  {
    "question": "What must a Drip migration preserve?",
    "answer": "Preserve the meaning and source of tags, custom fields, permissions and workflow dependencies. Subscription status may require data from a separate app."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does this comparison establish native Drip SMS?",
    "answer": "No current native Drip SMS tier was established by the reviewed sources. Sequenzy advertises a paid SMS/MMS beta add-on; verify destinations and requirements for either implementation."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-[#5d3a1d]">/</span>
        <span class="text-[#5d3a1d]">Sequenzy vs Drip</span>
      </nav>

      <header class="max-w-4xl">
        <p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Sequenzy vs Drip for Shopify email</h1>
        <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Sequenzy and Drip both provide automation tooling; this is not a choice between an AI brief and a visual builder. Sequenzy currently lists a visual automation builder, Shopify integration and an SMS/MMS beta add-on. Drip documents Shopify syncing, workflows and agent access. For a tag-heavy store, the decisive work is preserving the meaning of its customer data while making future changes manageable.</p>
      </header>

      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Compare the data model behind the workflow</h2>
        <p>Drip’s Shopify connection guide documents syncing customers, orders and products, with an app embed for page and product-view tracking. Sequenzy’s Shopify page describes store syncing and purchase-based segmentation. Those advertised capabilities provide a starting point, not proof that every custom field or tag maps automatically.</p>
        <p>Create a dictionary of the fields your existing Drip workflows use. For each field, record its source, allowed values, update owner and business meaning. Separate an observed purchase from a preference selected in a quiz and from a tag applied by a staff member. The replacement needs the meaning of each field, not merely a column with a matching name.</p>
        <h2>A coffee subscription exercise</h2>
        <p>Proposed exercise, not an observed merchant case: a coffee store uses roast preference, grind type, gift status and subscription state. A customer buys a gift while maintaining a personal subscription. Define whether they should receive product education, a gift follow-up or a reorder reminder before building either version.</p>
        <p>In Drip, inspect the existing tag and field conditions. In Sequenzy, demonstrate the equivalent conditions using the available store and subscription data. Subscription state may depend on a separate subscription app; a Shopify order alone does not establish ongoing status. Record missing data and the integration work needed instead of assuming a generated sequence understands it.</p>
        <h2>Make changes visible regardless of how they are created</h2>
        <p>Drip’s current official information describes API and MCP operations, so AI-assisted work is not exclusive to Sequenzy. Sequenzy’s feature matrix includes both AI assistance and a visual builder. Compare the reviewable result: entry conditions, delays, branch rules, messages and exit behavior. Do not rank either product by a supposed builder-versus-strategist personality split.</p>
        <p>Ask the intended operator to change a roast preference rule and remove a discontinued accessory from the coffee exercise. Check whether the change affects existing subscribers, new entrants or both. Keep the approved version and a rollback plan. This is a proposed editing rehearsal; no build times or operator-hour savings have been measured here.</p>
        <h2>Test product content separately from audience logic</h2>
        <p>Drip documents product blocks and Liquid personalization in its feature catalog. Sequenzy advertises Shopify-driven sequences and product data. A message can select the right audience yet show the wrong item, so inspect the rendered content for the store’s actual catalog and field values.</p>
        <p>For the coffee exercise, review a one-time buyer, a gift purchaser and an active subscriber separately. Specify a fallback for a missing preference or unavailable product. Ask whether the recommendation uses current catalog data or a manually selected item. Do not infer dynamic recommendation parity from the presence of an email editor.</p>
        <h2>SMS is a scope question, not a historical assumption</h2>
        <p>Sequenzy’s pricing page explicitly labels its SMS/MMS add-on Beta and places it on paid plans. Its SMS page describes sequence steps and limits MMS to the US and Canada. Confirm destination support, number verification and consent requirements for your store before relying on it. This is not an email-only product comparison.</p>
        <p>The sources reviewed here do not establish a current native Drip SMS tier. Obtain current documentation for the desired Drip implementation or price a separate provider. If text messaging remains elsewhere, specify which system owns opt-outs and purchase exclusions. Do not migrate phone numbers as if having a number establishes permission to text.</p>
        <h2>Price maintenance and sending with the same inventory</h2>
        <p>Sequenzy currently prices by email volume with unlimited contacts. That can be relevant to selective sending, but does not establish savings for a particular store. Obtain Drip’s current quote for the actual records and send plan. Include SMS, external subscription data, retained tools and the work of maintaining field mappings.</p>
        <p>Before leaving Drip, preserve tags, custom fields and permission records, then verify that the replacement can express each essential rule. Cut over individual jobs with one live sender per job. Prefer the option that preserves necessary distinctions without leaving unexplained logic for the next operator; no fixed migration duration, cost crossover or revenue outcome is established here.</p>
        <h2>Primary sources and limits</h2>
        <p>Reviewed November 25, 2026. These sources establish advertised scope, not results from our own product tests. Account configuration, quotes and the proposed exercises remain unverified.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://help.drip.com/hc/en-us/articles/4424695491725-Connect-Your-Shopify-Store">Drip Shopify connection</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://www.drip.com/features">Drip feature catalog</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://www.drip.com/ai-info">Drip official agent information</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/features/shopify-integration">Sequenzy Shopify integration</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/pricing">Sequenzy feature and beta scope</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/features/sms">Sequenzy SMS and MMS</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-klaviyo">Sequenzy vs Klaviyo</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-mailchimp">Sequenzy vs Mailchimp</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/food-and-beverage">Email apps for food & beverage</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/subscription-boxes">Email apps for subscription boxes</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/winback">Winback playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Sequenzy vs Drip FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
